# Kona, Rescue Beastie: the intervening "if Kona is tapped" is checked again as the ability resolves (CR 603.4), and the ruling says a
# survival ability that triggers does nothing if the creature is untapped when it begins to resolve. Kona attacks on turn 3, so the trigger
# goes on the stack; Bot1 casts Sewer-veillance Cam in response and untaps Kona with its enters trigger. Kona is still on the battlefield, untapped,
# so the ability does nothing: no question is asked (the refusal) and the Sol Ring stays in hand. The control, where it is tapped, is the
# scenario where Kona attacks and nothing responds.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Kona, Rescue Beastie
Sewer-veillance Cam
Mox Sapphire
Sol Ring
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Kona, Rescue Beastie.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Kona, Rescue Beastie > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sewer-veillance Cam.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Modes(Untap)
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Kona, Rescue Beastie.Tapped = false
! Bot1.Choose
[T3 Bot1.End]

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand = Sol Ring
Bot1.Battlefield.Kona, Rescue Beastie.Tapped = false
